## SQ-OB-01 | no script error on the batch's food items
@group B, fresh world
@commands Boot to `Done (`; `grep -E "Error occurred while handling event\|Exception" logs/kubejs/*.log logs/latest.log \| grep -iE "corn\|pie\|patty\|biscuit\|glazed\|salt\|summerhat\|farmers_hats"`
@pass Nothing printed; no startup script error
@fails Read the failing script named in the line; the batch touched `cd_food.js`, `effect_swaps.js`, `item_dict.js`, corn and veggiesdelight recipes
@from batches/r1111/bw.qb
shell grep -E "Error occurred while handling event|Exception" logs/kubejs/*.log logs/latest.log | grep -iE "corn|pie|patty|biscuit|glazed|salt|summerhat|farmers_hats" | head -5 | cut -c1-300; true
look nothing printed

## SQ-OB-02 | display names after /dumpall
@group client
@commands Client row: the names come from client lang scripts (`names.js`, `namechanges.js`), not visible to a server (r1112, r1115). `/kubejs dump_registry minecraft:item`; in JEI data or `kubejs/exported/display_names.json` after `/dumpall` check names
@pass `vintagedelight:salt_dust` is Salt; `corn_delight:corn` is Corn; spool is Spool of String; veggie patties are Veggie Patty
@fails Lang not picked up: check jar order and `names.js` gating
@from batches/r1111/bw.qb
> dumpall
waitlog \[dumpall\].*(ok|done) 900
shell python3 -c 'import json;d=json.load(open("kubejs/exported/display_names.json"));d=d.get("items",d) if isinstance(d,dict) else d;ids=["vintagedelight:salt_dust","corn_delight:corn"];print({k:(d.get(k) if isinstance(d,dict) else None) for k in ids});print([(k,v) for k,v in (d.items() if isinstance(d,dict) else []) if "spool" in k or "patty" in k][:10])'
look salt dust Salt; corn Corn; spool Spool of String; veggie patties Veggie Patty

## SQ-OB-03 | farmers_hats tag (hearthandharvest namespace): no summer hat
@group B
@commands `/zq itemtag hearthandharvest:farmers_hats`
@pass Contains the H&H hat, Wardrobe hat, Vinery straw hat, Simple Hats farmerbrim; no `simplehats:summerhat`
@fails Tag script not applied
@from batches/r1112/rowtext.qb passed
> zq itemtag hearthandharvest:farmers_hats
waitlog \[zq\] done 20
expect farmers_hats .*hearthandharvest:farmers_hat
expect farmers_hats .*wardrobe:farmers_hat_helmet
expect farmers_hats .*vinery:straw_hat
expect farmers_hats .*simplehats:farmerbrim
reject farmers_hats .*summerhat

## SQ-OB-04 | fruit pies and a Rustic cheesecake take 3 fruit; filling cans unchanged (one narrow query per pie)
@group B
@commands Every fruit pie recipe via `/kubejs dump_recipes` grep `pie`; check apple, pumpkin, sweet berry, grape pie and a Rustic cheesecake
@pass Each takes 3 fruit; filling cans unchanged
@fails Recipe still on 2: `pieBake` call site
@from batches/r1112/b_vh.qb
> zq rdetail creativedelight:baking/apple_pie
> zq rdetail creativedelight:baking/pumpkin_pie
> zq rdetail creativedelight:baking/sweet_berry_cheesecake
> zq rdetail creativedelight:baking/grape_pie
> zq rdetail creativedelight:baking/syrup_cheesecake
> zq rdetail canned_apple_pie_filling_pot
> zq rdetail canned_pumpkin_pie_filling_pot
> zq rdetail canned_sweet_berry_pie_filling_pot
expect baking/apple_pie \{\S+\} -> 1 apple_pie <- farmersdelight:pie_crust
expect baking/grape_pie \{\S+\} -> 1 grape_pie <- farmersdelight:pie_crust
expect baking/syrup_cheesecake \{\S+\} -> 1 syrup_cheesecake <- farmersdelight:pie_crust
look each pie and the cheesecake: crust + 3 of its fruit + 2 sweet (pumpkin_pie: 3 pumpkin slices, grape: 3 grapes, syrup cheesecake: 3 syrup); the _from_filling recipes are crust + can; the three canned_*_pie_filling_pot recipes keep 3 fruit + 2 sweet + empty can (unchanged)

